KNOWNBUG: N5008 [class.base.init]/6 -- delegating-constructor
recognition is declaration-order dependent: a delegating constructor
declared BEFORE its target is not recognized (constructor components
not yet visible to the detector), so members are default-initialized
instead; with a non-default-constructible member this is a hard
CONVERSION ERROR ("found no match" for a zero-argument constructor).
Root cause of the goto_program.cpp dog-food failure
(goto_programt::instructiont's delegating default constructor).
g++/clang++ runtime-verified.  Flip to CORE when fixed.
